  "issue_number": 7874,
  "issue_title": "GraphQL parity: sudo field missing block_start/block_end/from/to filters",
  "issue_body": "**Mirror this exactly:** MCP tool `get_sudo` in `src/mcp-server.mjs`, which already implements this exact filter set.\n\n## Context\n\nGraphQL's `sudo` field is missing `block_start`, `block_end`, `from`, `to` \u2014 all supported by `GET /api/v1/sudo` and by MCP's `get_sudo`.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Add `block_start: Int, block_end: Int, from: String, to: String` arguments to the `sudo` field in `src/graphql.mjs`.\n- Resolver passes them through to the same loader the MCP tool uses.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- [ ] `sudo` field accepts `block_start`, `block_end`, `from`, `to` matching REST.\n- [ ] Test coverage: a block-range filter and a time-range filter.\n\n## Expected Outcome\n\nA GraphQL client can filter sudo events by block/time range, matching REST and MCP.\n\n## Links & Resources\n\n- REST route: `GET /api/v1/sudo`.\n- MCP tool: `get_sudo`, `src/mcp-server.mjs`.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-24T20:13:42.000Z",
